    "body": "Our recent manual-test work exposed a concrete reason this integration matters: identifying the right CDC configuration/interface/alternate can require walking USB descriptors, while the high-level Serial API hides that topology.\n\nA shared device identity layer could solve more than chooser UX: it could let an application determine that a `SerialPort`, `HIDDevice`, and `USBDevice` refer to the same physical/composite USB device without forcing the site to reimplement descriptor matching.\n\nThat same identity primitive could also help #161 and Serial #128.\n",
